{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_security_stack", "label": "Recommended middleware stack and its ordering", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "requestId outermost so every log line including errors has an id; securityHeaders above everything that rejects so those responses carry them; cors outside auth because preflights are anonymous by spec; handleErrors outside csrf so it maps that middleware own 403, and inside the header layers so what it returns still flows through them; fallback at the root."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_requestid", "label": "requestId()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_securityheaders", "label": "securityHeaders() / withSecurityHeaders", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The middleware covers its own subtree including an HttpError thrown below it, but never a response raised outside that subtree \u2014 the backend own 404, the 413, the generic 500. Configure it on the server when the whole server needs it, as middleware when only a subtree does."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_nosniff_default", "label": "X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff on by default", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Written by the backend rather than a middleware, so it also reaches responses no middleware sees. It is the only default because it is the only header of the bundle that cannot change how an existing application is embedded, framed or referred to \u2014 X-Frame-Options and Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy would break iframes and OAuth popups, so they stay opt-in."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_cors", "label": "cors(...)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_csrfprotection", "label": "csrfProtection(...)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Browser apps only, after CORS and before handlers; its cookie uses the __Host- prefix by default and is deliberately not HttpOnly because double-submit needs JS to read it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_requesttimeout", "label": "requestTimeout(ms)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_handleerrors", "label": "handleErrors / withErrorHandler", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Return a generic body and log the detail server-side keyed by the request id; keep 403 and 404 unspecific."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_serializecookie", "label": "serializeCookie", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Strict by omission \u2014 an unmentioned attribute resolves to Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Path=/ \u2014 so the two-argument call is already shippable and loosening is what you write down. Path is always emitted because otherwise the browser derives scope from the request URI. It refuses a Path or Domain that could break out, since both reach the header verbatim and the last Domain is the one that counts."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_host_cookie_prefix", "label": "__Host- cookie prefix", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Requires Secure, Path=/ and no Domain; it is what stops a sibling subdomain from planting a token."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_trustedproxies", "label": "Trusting client IPs / trustedProxies", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Does my proxy overwrite the header is the wrong question \u2014 NGINX, AWS ALB and Cloudflare all append, so the client own text stays at the left of the chain forever. Name the proxies and resolve from the socket end inwards, the only end infrastructure controls."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_redirect_same_origin", "label": "redirect() is same-origin only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An absolute URL, a protocol-relative //host or a control character throws HttpError(400), so forwarding a ?next= parameter fails closed instead of becoming an open redirect."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_redirectexternal", "label": "redirectExternal(...)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The same helper without the origin rule; being a separate name makes every deliberate off-origin hop greppable in one command."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_redacturlcredentials", "label": "redactUrlCredentials / redactedUrlLabel", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The server-side copy needs hygiene too \u2014 a password that has reached a log aggregator has to be rotated, not deleted."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_input_caps", "label": "Capping untrusted input", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Request bodies at 1 MiB on every backend, refused with 413 before the handler and without consulting withErrorHandler because a size cap is a transport decision; WebSocket frames at maxFrameBytes; untrusted HTML escaped; and responses you fetch are untrusted input too \u2014 a Content-Length is a claim rather than a limit and a chunked response declares none."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_client_bounds", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_input_caps", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/security.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_security_stack", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_security_requestid", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/security.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_s